  "notes": [
    "Runtime: the gated e1a79c1ce9 build (patches 0036 and 0037). 0037: lean_wasm_compile, the one-shot compile behind snapshot probes and compiler batteries, now reports every message of the tasks a command starts (Elab.async proofs, kernel checks, linters) once each, in the native frontend's order. Before, a false proof elaborated with Elab.async, such as one run by lean4game's GameServer Runner, compiled with errors=0. The call now returns only after every task still recorded for a command has finished, so call it on a thread that can block and supervise it with a wall-clock limit. 0036 (deep recursion fails with Lean's error at the browser engine's stack limit) is unchanged from lean-v4.34.0-41ec565.",
    "Runtime-only release: lean-core, mathlib-essential and mathlib-game-extra are byte-identical to lean-v4.34.0-a8817d0's and lean-v4.34.0-41ec565's (transport copied, not re-packed); native64 and the lists are the import's. Apps re-pair (rebake snapshots) against this runtime's build id.",
    "Since the import, patches 0034 (Lean/Environment, Elab/Import, Language/Lean, Shell), 0036 (Lean/CoreM: two new functions) and 0037 (Lean/Shell: wasmCompile's loop) changed stdlib sources, so the browser packs' oleans of those modules predate them until the next import. This is harmless: the runtime runs its own compiled code for them. Against the import build, only those modules' generated C differs: 0036 only added names, and 0037 renumbered Shell's private specializations, none reused and none referenced from any other module. lean-lib is the e1a79c1ce9 build's own lib/lean, the tree the release gate passed on."
  ],
